{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "pmis-notification-service-2026",
    "name": "PMIS Notification Service (port 8002)",
    "description": "Postman collection for PMIS-notification-service — the email/SMS/OTP dispatch + notification-template master microservice running on port 8002.\n\n**Endpoints covered:**\n- `GET /health`\n- Email dispatch: `POST /notifications/email/send`\n- SMS dispatch: `POST /notifications/sms/send`\n- OTP: `POST /notifications/otp/send`, `POST /notifications/otp/verify`\n- Master data: `GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/v3/master/notification_templates/*` (Bearer-protected — needs a JWT minted by user-mgmt on port 8001)\n\n**Two ways to use this collection:**\n1. **Direct (port 8002)** — set `baseUrl` to `http://10.1.131.199:8002`. Hits notification-service directly. Master endpoints require `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` from a user-mgmt login.\n2. **Through monolith proxy** — set `baseUrl` to `http://10.1.131.199:8000` AND ensure the monolith has `NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_PROXY_ENABLED=true`. The monolith's `NotificationServiceProxyMiddleware` (doc 38) forwards `/api/v3/master/notification_templates/*` here transparently.\n\nLogin to obtain `accessToken` is done against user-mgmt — see `PMIS_User_Service.postman_collection.json`. The same JWT works here because both services share `SECRET_KEY`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Cron",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Daily deadline-digest cron",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Cron-Secret",
                "value": "{{cronSharedSecret}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/notifications/cron/daily-digest",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "notifications",
                "cron",
                "daily-digest"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Scans the shared ``pmis_db`` for milestones / activities ending within DEADLINE_WINDOW_DAYS (default 5) OR already past due, groups them per responsible user (org_admin / project_admin / project_member scoped to the project), and sends one email per user via the existing dispatch + SMTP pipeline.\n\n**Auth:** ``X-Cron-Secret`` header matching the ``CRON_SHARED_SECRET`` env var on the notification-service container. Empty / unset secret → 503 (endpoint disabled). Wrong / missing header → 401.\n\n**Body:** all fields optional. Leave empty for the normal daily run. Override ``today`` (ISO date) to replay a specific day; override ``windowDays`` (0-30) to widen / narrow the look-ahead for one call.\n\n**Response:** ``{ranAt, usersNotified, emailsSent, emailsFailed, itemsAggregated}``.\n\nAdd a ``X-Cron-Secret`` header manually before sending.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"today\": \"\",\n  \"windowDays\": 5\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ],
      "description": "Endpoints called by the DevOps host cron once a day. Gated by the ``X-Cron-Secret`` header that must match ``CRON_SHARED_SECRET`` env var on the notification-service container."
    },
    {
      "name": "Health & Root",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Service health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns service status, configured email_provider, and sms_provider."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Email Notifications",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send an email notification",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notifications/email/send",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "notifications",
                "email",
                "send"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sends an email through the provider configured in EMAIL_PROVIDER (smtp/sendgrid).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"to\": [\"user@example.com\"],\n  \"subject\": \"Welcome to PMIS\",\n  \"body\": \"<h1>Hello</h1><p>Welcome to the PMIS portal.</p>\",\n  \"is_html\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "SMS Notifications",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Send an SMS notification",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notifications/sms/send",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "notifications",
                "sms",
                "send"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Sends an SMS through the provider configured in SMS_PROVIDER (twilio/msg91/mock).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"to\": \"+919999999999\",\n  \"message\": \"Your PMIS appointment is confirmed.\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "OTP",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Generate and send an OTP via SMS or Email",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notifications/otp/send",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "notifications",
                "otp",
                "send"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Generates a numeric OTP and delivers it through the chosen channel.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"channel\": \"sms\",\n  \"destination\": \"+919999999999\",\n  \"purpose\": \"verification\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Verify a previously sent OTP",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/notifications/otp/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "notifications",
                "otp",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Verifies a previously sent OTP for the given channel + destination.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"channel\": \"sms\",\n  \"destination\": \"+919999999999\",\n  \"otp\": \"123456\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Master Data — Notification Templates",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List notification templates",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v3/master/notification_templates?include_inactive=false",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v3",
                "master",
                "notification_templates"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "include_inactive",
                  "value": "false",
                  "description": "Set true to include soft-deactivated rows"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "List notification templates. Requires master_data:view permission."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get a notification template",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v3/master/notification_templates/{template_id}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v3",
                "master",
                "notification_templates",
                ":template_id"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "template_id",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Numeric notification_template id"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fetch a single notification template by id. Requires master_data:view."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Create a notification template",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v3/master/notification_templates/create",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v3",
                "master",
                "notification_templates",
                "create"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Create a new notification template. Requires master_data:manage. Channel must be 'email' or 'sms'; subject required for email, omitted for sms. Placeholder allow-list is enforced for known kinds (otp_login, password_reset_link, password_reset_otp).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"templateKind\": \"otp_login\",\n  \"channel\": \"email\",\n  \"subject\": \"Your PMIS login code\",\n  \"body\": \"<p>Your code is {code}. It expires in {ttl_minutes} minutes.</p>\",\n  \"isHtml\": true,\n  \"description\": \"Custom OTP login template\",\n  \"active\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Update a notification template",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v3/master/notification_templates/{template_id}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v3",
                "master",
                "notification_templates",
                ":template_id"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "template_id",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Numeric notification_template id"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Patch the editable fields of a notification template. Requires master_data:manage. Channel/kind are immutable here — to change them, deactivate and create a new row.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"subject\": \"Updated subject\",\n  \"body\": \"<p>Updated body with {code} and {ttl_minutes} minutes.</p>\",\n  \"description\": \"Updated description\",\n  \"active\": true\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Soft-deactivate a notification template",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v3/master/notification_templates/{template_id}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v3",
                "master",
                "notification_templates",
                ":template_id"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "template_id",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Numeric notification_template id"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Soft-deactivate (active=false) a notification template. Rows are never hard-deleted. Requires master_data:manage."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Re-activate a soft-disabled notification template",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v3/master/notification_templates/{template_id}/restore",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v3",
                "master",
                "notification_templates",
                ":template_id",
                "restore"
              ],
              "variable": [
                {
                  "key": "template_id",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Numeric notification_template id"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Re-activate a previously soft-deactivated template. 409 if another active row already covers the same (kind, channel)."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8002",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Notification-service base URL. Use http://10.1.131.199:8002 for the deployed instance, or http://10.1.131.199:8000 (with NOTIFICATION_SERVICE_PROXY_ENABLED=true on the monolith) to go through the proxy."
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "JWT access token minted by user-mgmt's POST /api/v3/users/login. Required for /api/v3/master/notification_templates/* — unprotected endpoints (email/sms/otp dispatch + /health) ignore this."
    }
  ]
}